{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":486590,"name":"Philippe Wong","username":"Philippe_Wong","avatar_template":"https://avatars.discourse-cdn.com/v4/letter/p/e19adc/{size}.png","created_at":"2026-09-08T15:25:25.405Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486590-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486590-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486590-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486590-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery one of my Grok Bots fails with “Bot failed to respond,” including a simple health check that uses no tools, connectors, search, memory, or files.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eDetails:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot for macOS, version 0.44.0, Stable track\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eApp is fully up to date\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eFully quitting with Cmd+Q and reopening did not resolve it\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eBot roster and conversation history remain visible\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eApproximate start: September 7, 2026, around 5:29 PM MYT (UTC+8)\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRequest ID: 7c3fcc19-f7c9-4f21-afa5-9adc5a599ca3\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI tried “Update Grok’s Computer” but not Reset because the workspace contains important recent files and I want to avoid losing changes. After selecting that, I seem to have “Backup not ready” as a new status that’s been stuck that way for a while.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI posted the issue on similar topic another user shared but haven’t had a response, figured it might be best to create a new topic.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eExcited to get the ball rolling with my Grok Bots, hope to resolve this issue soon especially since it happened whilst I was still setting things up and only a few days after subscribing.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486590-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486590-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis is the first bug and I haven’t been able to do anything else after.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt happened after I gave it a long instruction with a ZIP file.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486590-operating-system-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486590-operating-system-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486590-version-information-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486590-version-information-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVersion: 0.44.0\u003cbr\u003e\nRelease Track: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: darwin\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486590-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486590-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eRequest ID: 7c3fcc19-f7c9-4f21-afa5-9adc5a599ca3\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486590-additional-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486590-additional-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI haven’t downloaded nor tried using Cursor. So the choices below “Does this stop you from using Cursor” is not relevant to me. I picked “Yes - Cursor is unusable” since I am required to pick an option.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-486590-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-486590-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eYes - Cursor is unusable\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":2,"updated_at":"2026-09-08T15:36:55.180Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":8,"reads":5,"readers_count":4,"score":41.0,"yours":false,"topic_id":171058,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-bot-failed-to-respond","display_username":"Philippe Wong","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":136583,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-bot-failed-to-respond/171058/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":486921,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-09T01:47:03.197Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHi \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/philippe_wong\"\u003e@Philippe_Wong\u003c/a\u003e , thanks for the detailed report.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI checked your account, and the affected Grok Bot computer has now been rebuilt from its saved data. It is online, and the stored data is present. This was not caused by your Mac, the app update, or the ZIP file.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ePlease reopen Grok Bot and try sending a short message. You do not need to use Reset or Update. If it still fails, let me 